WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.901
Calibration means matching confidence to actual knowledge, skill, accuracy, or likelihood.

00:00:03.901 --> 00:00:06.665
Good calibration does not mean always being uncertain.

00:00:06.665 --> 00:00:09.430
It means confidence rises and falls with evidence.

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:13.922
If you are highly confident, you should be able to point to why.

00:00:13.922 --> 00:00:17.032
If evidence is weak, confidence should be more cautious.

00:00:17.032 --> 00:00:21.524
Calibration helps people decide when to act, check, learn, or ask for help.

00:00:21.524 --> 00:00:24.979
Overconfidence is risky because it can stop checking too early.

00:00:24.979 --> 00:00:27.398
A person may skip testing, ignore feedback,

00:00:27.398 --> 00:00:30.163
or dismiss uncertainty because the answer feels obvious.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.890
Underconfidence is also a problem.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:35.691
It can prevent people from using real capability, taking appropriate action,

00:00:35.691 --> 00:00:37.073
or accepting useful challenge.

00:00:37.073 --> 00:00:42.257
Both problems distort performance because confidence no longer matches what the person can actually do.

00:00:42.257 --> 00:00:44.675
Prediction checks are a simple calibration tool.

00:00:44.675 --> 00:00:48.822
Estimate how likely an answer is, how well you understand a topic,

00:00:48.822 --> 00:00:51.241
or how successful an approach will be.

00:00:51.241 --> 00:00:53.660
Then compare the estimate with the result.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.387
Confidence ratings can also help.

00:00:55.387 --> 00:00:58.152
Before submitting an answer or making a decision,

00:00:58.152 --> 00:01:00.571
rate your confidence and note the evidence.

00:01:00.571 --> 00:01:03.681
Over time, you can see whether confidence is reliable.

00:01:03.681 --> 00:01:07.136
Feedback loops improve calibration when they are specific and timely.

00:01:07.136 --> 00:01:09.900
The point is not to punish being wrong.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.010
The point is to update beliefs based on evidence.

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:18.539
Accurate self-assessment improves learning and decision quality because it helps you choose the right next action:

00:01:18.539 --> 00:01:22.340
continue, review, practice, test, slow down, or bring in another perspective.
